  ('Carringtons Wines & Spirits', 'WINE MERCHANT', '{}', 2, 'chorlton', 'manchester', 53.435, -2.2765, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Ciaran and Michael Keaney have spent thirty years building direct relationships with producers on Barlow Moor Road — a Decanter regional Wine Retailer of the Year that still lets you just ask Ross what''s good this week.', '{"afternoon","evening"}', 64, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Sweet Mandarin', 'CANTONESE RESTAURANT', '{}', 3, 'northern-quarter', 'manchester', 53.4858, -2.2335, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Helen and Lisa Tse still cook their grandmother''s own recipes on Copperas Street, the ones that won them a place on BBC''s Dragons'' Den and a shelf of cookbooks since — twenty-plus years in, and the family never once franchised themselves out of the kitchen.', '{"evening","late"}', 78, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Dunham Massey', 'HISTORIC ESTATE', '{}', 1, 'altrincham', 'cheshire', 53.383, -2.4, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Three hundred acres of deer park and a Georgian hall the Earls of Stamford left exactly as lived-in as it was — the National Trust''s quietest big afternoon out within reach of the tram line.', '{"morning","afternoon"}', 72, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Weaver Hall Museum & Workhouse', 'HERITAGE CENTRE', '{}', 1, 'northwich', 'cheshire', 53.2575, -2.5195, false, '{none}', '{}', 'A former workhouse that now tells Northwich''s own story plainly — salt, boatbuilding and the chemical works that actually built the town, run by the council that still means it, not dressed up for a brochure.', '{"morning","afternoon"}', 56, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('MADS Little Theatre', 'PERFORMING ARTS', '{}', 1, 'macclesfield', 'cheshire', 53.2596, -2.1281, false, '{none}', '{}', 'The Macclesfield Amateur Dramatic Society built their own 193-seat house out of a Sunday school on Lord Street and have been filling it since 1947 — five or six main-stage runs a year, no understudy pretending otherwise.', '{"evening"}', 62, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Brook Lane Coffee Co', 'COFFEE ROOM', '{}', 2, 'alderley-edge', 'cheshire', 53.299, -2.228, false, '{none}', '{}', 'A locally roasted bean and an unhurried pace just off the village centre — Alderley Edge''s actual neighbourhood coffee house, a few minutes from every cocktail bar that''s opened and closed on London Road since.', '{"morning","afternoon"}', 56, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Indique', 'INDIAN RESTAURANT', '{}', 3, 'didsbury', 'manchester', 53.4263, -2.2422, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Dinesh Maheshwari built this on dishes from his own Rajasthan, not a laminated curry-house card — a Travellers'' Choice regular on Burton Road that a couple marked a farewell meal at after seven years of coming back.', '{"afternoon","evening"}', 74, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-10 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Hack Green Secret Nuclear Bunker', 'HERITAGE CENTRE', '{}', 1, 'nantwich', 'cheshire', 53.0268, -2.5307, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Three and a half acres built underground to run the North West through a nuclear war that never came, on a lane outside Nantwich — still owned by the family who opened it to the public, and the control room hasn''t been redressed for visitors.', '{"morning","afternoon"}', 58, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-11 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Bullring Cocktail Bar', 'COCKTAIL BAR', '{}', 2, 'northwich', 'cheshire', 53.2595, -2.513, false, '{none}', '{}', 'A former building society office off the Bullring turned gin-heavy cocktail room, sister to the Salthouse a few doors down — Friday and Saturday only, and the quiz nights are the reason regulars still show up early.', '{"evening","late"}', 64, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-11 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Fiveclouds Tap & Bottle', 'BOTTLE SHOP', '{}', 2, 'macclesfield', 'cheshire', 53.2612, -2.1254, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Ten keg lines and one cask straight from Fiveclouds'' own mash tun, on Market Place with nothing on the menu beyond crisps and bar snacks — which is rather the point.', '{"afternoon","evening","late"}', 70, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-11 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Watergate Street Gallery', 'ART GALLERY', '{}', 2, 'chester', 'cheshire', 53.1898, -2.894, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Thirty-odd years on Watergate Street showing original, affordably priced work — bold and colourful on purpose, and the gallery still wants you to argue about it rather than just admire it quietly.', '{"morning","afternoon"}', 68, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-11 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('That Beer Place', 'BOTTLE SHOP', '{}', 2, 'chester', 'cheshire', 53.1917, -2.8836, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Lisa and Dale Lord''s own cellar of three hundred-plus craft beers and sixty-odd ciders on Foregate Street, reigning CAMRA National Cider and Perry Pub of the Year — no keg lager in sight, and no apology for it.', '{"afternoon","evening"}', 73, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-11 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Vin Santo', 'WINE BAR', '{}', 2, 'chester', 'cheshire', 53.19, -2.8924, false, '{none}', '{}', 'A six-hundred-year-old crypted cellar under Watergate Street, poured by the glass or sold by the bottle to take home — Simon''s own tastings run on wines you won''t find lit up behind a bar anywhere else in the city.', '{"afternoon","evening","late"}', 75, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-11 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Mielle', 'COFFEE ROOM', '{}', 2, 'ancoats', 'manchester', 53.48494, -2.228206, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Paul and his wife''s own pastry kitchen took over the wine merchant''s old retail wall in July, matcha tarts by day and a sake-and-cocktail bar once the patisserie case empties out.', '{"morning","afternoon","evening"}', 78, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-12 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('George Charles', 'GASTROPUB', '{}', 2, 'didsbury', 'manchester', 53.4245, -2.246, false, '{none}', '{}', 'A corner shop since the 1880s, named for the greengrocer who ran it, now pulling local ales for a Burton Road crowd that didn''t expect the kitchen to be this good.', '{"morning","afternoon","evening"}', 76, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-12 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Morgan Edwards', 'WINE MERCHANT', '{}', 3, 'knutsford', 'cheshire', 53.303, -2.3735, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Started out of a stall in the market hall in 2018 and earned the move to King Street — a shelf of small-producer wine and rare whisky that rewards asking the owners rather than just browsing.', '{"afternoon","evening"}', 70, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-12 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Liquor and Co', 'SPEAKEASY', '{}', 3, 'chester', 'cheshire', 53.1902, -2.893, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Upstairs on Watergate Street behind a door that still looks like it isn''t one, with a hidden room most first-timers never find — sister to Craft & Company, built on the same unhurried pour.', '{"evening","late"}', 79, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-12 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Atlas Bar', 'GIN BAR', '{}', 2, 'deansgate', 'manchester', 53.4725, -2.2512, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Mark and Elaine Wrigley''s gin wall has grown past 570 bottles since they took the place over in 2012, directly across from the tram and train and in front of the towers, with no two regulars drinking quite the same thing.', '{"afternoon","evening","late"}', 81, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-12 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review'),
  ('Romazzino', 'ITALIAN RESTAURANT', '{}', 3, 'nantwich', 'cheshire', 53.0668, -2.5212, false, '{none}', '{}', 'Giuseppe and Peppe have run the pizza oven on the High Street since 2007, and the weekday Pranzo Completo still gets a proper two courses out the door faster than anywhere newer in town.', '{"afternoon","evening"}', 75, 'Not yet Gate 1 reviewed — raw daily research candidate, no independent verification pass has run on it.', null, null, null, '[{"note":"Raw daily-research candidate from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-12 — not yet independently re-verified by a second review pass. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb, 'pending_review');

insert into district_candidates (
  name, region, character, rationale, status, sources
) values
  ('Frodsham', 'cheshire', 'A sandstone market town where the Cheshire Plain meets the Mersey marshes — a wide Georgian high street, a weekly Thursday market that''s run since the 13th century, and the Sandstone Trail starting almost the moment the pavement does.', 'Found via this run''s required per-day new-district check, not user-named — a genuine gap surfaced while researching venue candidates elsewhere in Cheshire, not manufactured to fill the check. Frodsham is a genuinely distinct, well-documented Cheshire market town, consistently covered (Great British Life, Cheshire West and Chester''s own tourism copy, chesterstandard.co.uk) as a 13th-century market town with a wide Georgian Main Street, a weekly Thursday market and a monthly Artisan Market, real independent-shop density (''bursting with unique independent shops, exceptional cafés, restaurants and local services'' per visitcheshire.com), and Next Door — a Michelin-guide-featured restaurant in a 17th-century building run by the same family for three generations — plus Ristorante Lorenzo''s and Main Street Kitchen as further real, named independent dining. Also the signed gateway to the 34-mile Sandstone Trail along Cheshire''s Sandstone Ridge, a genuine Do-category draw none of this file''s other districts offer. Passes the ''would a local raise an eyebrow this isn''t already covered'' test the same way Prestbury/Knutsford/Cheadle Hulme/Lymm did. Distance check: roughly 9.1 miles (14.7km) from Northwich and 9.7 miles (15.6km) from Chester, the two nearest existing Cheshire districts — comfortably clear of both, sitting in the real gap between them rather than overlapping either (a different, further-out pairing than the Tarporley/Northwich corridor this file already added 2026-09-18, not a duplicate of that reasoning). Coordinates (53.294629/-2.72891) are Frodsham''s real town-centre/Main Street centroid, cross-checked across multiple independent mapping sources rather than invented; doogal.co.uk/api.postcodes.io were both blocked by the network egress proxy this session, so this is a web-search-derived figure rather than a direct geocode-API call, flagged for the reviewer to tighten if precise geocoding becomes available. accentColor (#9C8558, a muted sandstone-ochre nodding to the Sandstone Ridge/Trail identity specifically) checked for perceptual distinctness against every existing Cheshire accent, closest neighbours Knutsford''s sandy amber (#B8935C, notably lighter) and Nantwich''s faded brick-clay (#A56A52, notably pinker/redder) and Chester''s sandstone-red (#A6512F, notably more orange-red) — distinct from all three. base (54) is a reasoned estimate, similar register to Knutsford (54) and just below Nantwich (56) — a genuine working market town with real everyday commercial life, not a sleepy village. kind ''county'', matching every other Cheshire district. No district group added — Frodsham doesn''t fit the Golden Triangle''s real geography and a two-district group with Northwich/Tarporley would be grouping for its own sake rather than a real, named local identity, the same judgment already made when the Tarporley/Northwich corridor was added. No venues suggested for it in this same run — same ''district entry only, venues as separate follow-up work'' precedent every prior district promotion has followed; one note worth flagging for a future pass: Frodsham Golf Club (referenced in this file''s own venues.json _cheshireGolfClubsSource note) was independently confirmed permanently closed in 2022, so is not a candidate once this district exists.', 'pending_review', '[{"note":"Raw daily-research district candidate from docs/data/district-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-01 — not yet independently re-verified. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb),
  ('Sale', 'manchester', 'A shopping precinct that quietly turned into a food destination — restaurant numbers here grew faster since the pandemic than anywhere else in the city, Stanley Square doing the work a high street used to, with a Restaurant of the Year plaque in a bistro that nobody outside Trafford had heard of five years ago.', 'Found via this run''s required per-day new-district check, not user-named. Sale is a genuine, distinct Trafford town roughly 5 miles south-west of Manchester city centre, recently and repeatedly covered as its own named food destination rather than a residential commuter suburb: themanc.com''s own feature is titled ''A Manc''s guide to: Sale, a foodie neighbourhood reborn''; confidentials.com runs a dedicated ''insider''s guide to eating and drinking in Sale''; and coverage of the town cites a Guardian analysis finding restaurant numbers in Sale grew 43% since the pandemic — the highest increase of any area surveyed — plus a nomination for MFDF''s Foodie Neighbourhood of the Year. Named, verifiable independents anchor this: The Fat Loaf (2022 Restaurant of the Year, North West, at the Food Awards England), Hops and Boogie (an independent bottle shop/taproom/record store), and Stanley Square itself (the real, named former shopping precinct now doing double duty as the town''s food-and-drink hub) — passes the ''would a local raise an eyebrow this isn''t already covered'' test the same way Prestbury/Knutsford/Lymm/Ramsbottom did. Distance check: roughly 2.7 miles (4.3km) from Altrincham and 2 miles (3.3km) from Chorlton, the two nearest existing Manchester-metro districts — closer than most existing pairs in this file but not unprecedented (Heaton Moor/Stockport Underbanks sit a few hundred metres apart, Didsbury/Chorlton ~2.5km) and, more importantly, genuinely distinct in character from both: Altrincham''s is a market-town identity built around its own Market/Market House, Chorlton''s around Beech Road''s beer-mile/tapas-strip scene, Sale''s specifically around a reborn shopping-precinct-turned-food-hub with its own named press identity. Coordinates (53.4215/-2.3198) are Sale town centre/Stanley Square''s own area, independently verified via web search rather than invented; doogal.co.uk/api.postcodes.io were both blocked by the network egress proxy this session, so this is a web-search-derived figure rather than a direct geocode-API call, flagged for the reviewer to tighten if precise geocoding becomes available. accentColor (#8C6E4A, a muted toffee-brown) checked for perceptual distinctness against every existing Manchester-metro accent that would actually render alongside it at city zoom — closest neighbours Ancoats'' rust-brick (#9C5030, notably more orange-red) and Didsbury''s dusty rose (#B98098, a wholly different hue family) — distinct from both. base (74) is a reasoned estimate, just below Chorlton (78) and Didsbury (80) given Sale''s food scene is real but more recently arrived/still-rising per its own press coverage, and above Heaton Moor (68) given the scale of Stanley Square''s offer. kind ''city'', matching every other Manchester-metro district. No district group added — Sale doesn''t fit any existing group''s real geography (the Deansgate Spine and Ancoats & the NQ groups are both inner-city-core). No venues suggested for it in this same run — same ''district entry only, venues as separate follow-up work'' precedent every prior district promotion has followed; worth flagging for a future pass that two named venues found during this research (The Fat Loaf, Hops and Boogie) were not independently verified to Curia''s full Hard rule 1 bar here, since a venue can''t be suggested against a district id that doesn''t exist yet, and that the already-live/pending Libero (Altrincham) candidate''s own researchNotes separately reference its team opening a second, Sale-based venue (''Pray Tell'') — also not decided here.', 'pending_review', '[{"note":"Raw daily-research district candidate from docs/data/district-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-04 — not yet independently re-verified. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb),
  ('Marple', 'manchester', 'Sixteen locks climbing the Peak Forest Canal in one steep flight, Britain''s highest masonry-arch aqueduct carrying it over the Goyt a few minutes on, and a Bridgewater-adjacent high street that never quite got the chain-pub memo — a Stockport satellite that reads more Peak fringe than suburb.', 'Found via this run''s required per-day new-district check, not user-named — surfaced while researching Bramhall/Stockport Underbanks candidates elsewhere this session, not manufactured to fill the check. Marple is a genuinely distinct Stockport town at the edge of the Peak District, consistently covered as a real food-and-drink destination in its own right (ilovemanchester.com''s ''Marple is the jewel of the Cheshire Alps'') with a real independent scene verified this session: Traders (an independent micropub on Stockport Road running craft beer/wine/cocktails and foodie pop-ups), Fold in Marple Bridge (an independent bistro and bottle shop) and Angkor Soul (a Cambodian-influenced independent cafe) — none chain-owned per the sources checked. Its heritage draw is genuinely singular within this file: the Marple Locks flight (16 locks, one of the steepest in Britain, per Tripadvisor/Stockport Hub/Canal & River Trust coverage) and the Marple Aqueduct (the highest masonry-arch canal aqueduct in Britain, carrying the Peak Forest Canal over the River Goyt) — a real Do-category anchor no existing district shares, distinct from Stockport Underbanks'' market-hall/bank-vault identity and Bramhall''s village-green one. Passes the ''would a local raise an eyebrow this isn''t already covered'' test the same way Heaton Moor/Bramhall originally did. Distance check: roughly 4.9 miles (7.9km) from Bramhall and 3.9 miles (6.3km) from Stockport Underbanks, the two nearest existing districts — clearly distinct, comfortably past this file''s own close-adjacent precedent (Heaton Moor/Stockport Underbanks, a few hundred metres apart). Coordinates (53.395/-2.0677) are Marple town centre on Stockport Road, derived from this session''s SK6 postcode web-search results rather than invented; doogal.co.uk/api.postcodes.io were both blocked by the network egress proxy this session, so this is a web-search-derived figure, flagged for the reviewer to tighten if precise geocoding becomes available. Metro assigned ''manchester'' as Greater Manchester shorthand, the same judgment already applied to Stockport (Underbanks)/Heaton Moor/Cheadle Hulme/Bramhall. kind ''city'', matching every other Manchester-metro district. accentColor (#55666B, a cool gritstone slate-blue evoking the canal stonework and Peak District edge) checked for perceptual distinctness against every existing Manchester-metro accent that could render alongside it at city zoom — closest neighbours Heaton Moor''s dusty blue-grey (#6B7F94, notably lighter/more blue) and Spinningfields'' soft blue (#6E8FA6, a wholly different, brighter register) — distinct from both. base (60) is a reasoned estimate, below Heaton Moor (68) and Bramhall''s own real venue base scores, reflecting a real but smaller-scale independent cluster than either. No district group added — Marple doesn''t fit any existing group''s real geography. No venues suggested for it in this same run — same ''district entry only, venues as separate follow-up work'' precedent every prior district promotion has followed; Traders, Fold and Angkor Soul (named above) were not independently verified to Curia''s full Hard rule 1 bar here, since a venue can''t be suggested against a district id that doesn''t exist yet.', 'pending_review', '[{"note":"Raw daily-research district candidate from docs/data/district-suggestions.json, suggested 2026-10-06 — not yet independently re-verified. Synced 2026-10-12 for direct human review at /admin/review."}]'::jsonb);
